  "question_origin": "researcher_constructed",
  "question_text": "Fenora produces only wheat and books. The base year is 2025. In 2025 it produces 30 units of wheat at 4 currency units per unit and 10 books at 12 currency units each. In 2026 it produces 40 units of wheat at 5 currency units per unit and 12 books at 15 currency units each.\n\n(a) Calculate nominal GDP in 2026. Show your work.\n\n(b) Calculate real GDP in 2026 in base-year prices. Show your work.\n\n(c) Calculate the 2026 GDP deflator and the inflation rate from 2025 to 2026 using that deflator. Show your work.\n\n(d) A worker’s nominal wage is unchanged between 2025 and 2026. Based on the change in the price level, what happens to the purchasing power of that wage? Explain.\n\n(e) Draw a production possibilities curve with wheat and books on its axes. Show the effect of a technology improvement that raises productive capacity in both industries.",
